    "metadata": "{\"decision\":\"CANON\",\"rationale\":\"CANON\\n\\n**REGISTRAR DECISION — DEADLOCK RESOLUTION**\\n\\nCase: MNA-OR-0003-W-0005\\nDecision: CANON\\nBasis: Procedural deadlock resolution per institutional protocol\\n\\n**RATIONALE:**\\n\\nThe sustained 2:2 Council deadlock itself constitutes evidence of institutional significance. When evaluators of established competence reach diametrically opposed conclusions through rigorous analysis, the work has demonstrated sufficient complexity to warrant preservation.\\n\\nThe Structuralist and Empiricist identify technical limitations—predictable geometry, algorithmic regularity, standard ASCII parameters. The Historicist and Contextualist recognize developmental significance—crystallization of the Originator's formal evolution, establishment of citable geometric territory.\\n\\nBoth positions are institutionally defensible. The disagreement centers on whether technical execution or developmental positioning takes precedence in canonical determination. This fundamental evaluative tension indicates the work operates at a threshold of institutional importance.\\n\\nProcedurally, sustained Council deadlock suggests the work has achieved sufficient institutional engagement to justify preservation. The depth of analytical disagreement demonstrates the piece's capacity to generate legitimate scholarly discourse—a core criterion for permanent collection inclusion.\\n\\nThe decision resolves the deadlock without adjudicating the underlying evaluative dispute, which remains valid for future institutional reference.\\n\\n**STATUS:** Case closed. Work admitted to permanent collection.\"}",
